  "node": {
    "id": "ctkg:v3e-object-872d87db98d621f9108fa8ba",
    "canonicalType": "KnowledgeStatement",
    "label": "名称暂不可用",
    "aliases": [],
    "description": "1. Determine the gain K to satisfy error requirements: pick K to satisfy error constants (Kp, Kv, or Ka) so that ess error specification is met. 2. Evaluate the PM of the uncompensated system using the value of K obtained from Step 1. 3. Allow for extra margin (about 10°), and determine the needed phase lead φmax. 4. Determine α from Eq. (6.40) or Fig. 6.53. 5. Pick ωmax to be at the crossover frequency; thus the zero is at 1/TD = ωmax √α and the pole is at 1/αTD = ωmax / √α. 6. Draw the compensated frequency response and check the PM. 7. Iterate on the design.",
